AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAARRRRRRRRRGGGGGGGGGGGHHHHHHH!!!

It happened again.  One of the luckiest starts to a game ever.

Level 1: Found Crystal Plate Mail and Cloak of Displacement.
Level 2: Huge Ring shop.  Got a ring of conflict.  Three amulets
   also there.  Had no way to steal them, so I decided to come back
   later.  Also a like-aligned alter.
Level 3: Huge Scroll Shop. Lots of blessed identify scrolls.
Level 4: Large General store.

By level 4 I had a bit of money, so I went back to level 3, and 
bought all the identify scrolls.  Went back to level 2 and 
identified all the rings and amulets.  One was an amulet of life
saving.  I just didn't have enough money to buy it, and had
no way to steal it.

On my way over to the alter to sacrifice something, I accidentally
ran into a floating eye, and got paralysed.  A kobold appeared and
killed me.  Just like that.

-------------------------------------------------------------------

Brand new suggestion for nethack:  The ability to set a
monster_confirm option string.  I would set it to "ebjvF".
Then, before I attacked any e, b, j, v, or F, I would get
a message "WARNING -- Really Attack? [yn]"

It would save me a lot of grief early on in games.
Later in the game, when I was everything-resistant, and all
my armor and weapons were rustproof, I'd set it to NIL.

What does everyone else think?
